hello  i'm dr greg sadler and i would like to  tell you  about a new course a very short audio  course that i  have out on the listenable platform  called  basics of stoic philosophy and  practice and i i've designed it in such  a way  that you can listen to it on the go or  while you're working out while you're  doing other things  and you can learn exactly what it's  telling you about some of the bare bones  some of the basics  about who the stoics were and what  stoicism is all about  and it can be a great refresher for  people who already know something about  stoicism  you know can provoke some some thoughts  here and there about things they might  have  overlooked or forgotten about but it's  also for people who have no background  in stoicism at all but have heard about  it and want to understand  why hundreds of thousands of people  across the world  are studying and practicing stoicism  as a philosophy of life i'm going to  tell you about the course in just a  minute but before that  i want to say a little bit about  listenable as  a platform so what listenable offers  are audio courses that have  a number of lessons and the lessons are  anywhere from about 3 to 10 minutes long  so they're nice and short  you can listen to them sequentially you  can jump around in a course you can  focus in  on the topics that you are most  interested in you can go back to it over  and over again  and re-listen to any of the  courses that you want to and listenable  has a huge  range of material out there i've been  exploring it because they  gave me a like a 30-day trial thing for  creating a course and  you know there's there's quite a lot of  interesting content  they approached me because they they  knew i had the video channel  and the sadler's lecture podcast and  said would you like to do a course for  us  and i thought yeah i'll give it a shot  let's see how this goes  and you know i was very impressed by  their insistence  on producing really high quality  audio you know you have to record it all  in one  session so that it there's a consistency  of sound in the sound space that you  have  you write out scripts ahead of time  which is something kind of new  for me a new set of skills that i had to  develop but also good for thinking about  what you want to say  usually i'm actually just going as i am  right here  without any any major notes and just  talking directly to an audience but i  think there's something good about that  so i'm really excited to have this  course out i'm already plotting out my  next course  which will be on plato's symposium that  i will be developing for listenable so  let's talk about this course  what does the basics of stoic philosophy  and practice have  i've got a list here of the different  lessons first lesson just an  introduction of the class telling you  what we're going to be doing a little  bit about stoicism and  why it matters the second one is about  stoicism  uppercase s versus stoic stoicism  lowercase s a really important  distinction  something that many people are confused  about  and clarifying that we're going to be  doing the uppercase s  actual genuine stoic philosophy and  practices  the third lesson introduces you to some  of the main  uh thinkers writers practitioners of  stoicism  in the ancient times the people that  modern stoix themselves  are drawing upon then we jump right into  some  nuts and bolts core concepts we  focus on the stoic conception of  happiness or eudaimonia what is that  what are the stoics actually about what  is the  central goal for studying stoic  philosophy and  practicing it and applying it then we  talk about the good  the bad and this vast range of things  the stoics called the indifference this  is a key  idea of stoic ethical theory we talk  about a  very important concept the dichotomy of  control  the things we actually have control over  the things that we don't how to make  that distinction  what happens what goes right for us when  we do make that distinction properly  how we screw ourselves up when we we  don't then we jump into talking about  the four  cardinal virtues another really central  aspect to stoicism  what is wisdom what is justice what is  courage  what is temperance some people ask  questions like well i don't i don't see  kindness or gratitude in there they're  in there  you just gotta dig and that's what that  lesson is  is helping you to understand then we  delve into stoicism  and its theory of the emotions which  emotions do we want to  hold on to and prioritize like joy  love you know calmness all those sorts  of things which do we want to  try to eliminate like anger or envy or  irrational fear which of those do we  actually need to keep  but manage properly like rational fear  right  or rational desire so that's very  important  then we start looking at how stoicism  helps us to  widen our perspectives to look at  ourselves not just  as individuals but as members  of a community and extending that  community ultimately all the way out to  the cosmos thinking about things in in  space and time  we look at another really key set of  practices with examining expectations  and appearances  one of the ways in which practicing  stoicism helps us to  have a happier life is by learning to be  self-critical about the expectations  that we have  our responses to impressions and  appearances  not in a way that tears ourselves down  but in a way that allows us to live a  more  rational and grounded existence then we  move into how we rework habits and why  habits are so important what we're  aiming at  freedom and then finally we finish up by  talking about going back to the stoic  authors and talking about what text you  might want to  acquire and read and and which to start  out with i give you some  reading suggestions and i tell you why  you should check out this one  before this one so i'm really happy with  the way the course  came out the listenable people are very  happy on their end with  how the quality of the sound  and the instruction came together you  can check out the course for free  i'm going to include some links one link  is directly to the course where you can  go to it  there's already a lot of learners who  have gone through progress  through all the lessons that could be  you i'm also going to include an  affiliate link  so i do want to be very upfront about  this if you click the affiliate link and  you sign up for  for listenable i do get a little cut of  that  but it also gives you a 30 off thing  that gives you access not just to my  course but to a  whole plethora of other courses that you  might find interesting so i just wanted  to bring this to all of your attention  you can see the links below check out  the course if you think it's something  that you would like to do  go ahead and follow through and start  learning about stoicism today or if  you're already an old hand at it  do some refreshers  you

